# Act 1: Cast On. The format is described at the top of scripts/story.gd.
# Flow (Alex's design, 2026-11-12; every line here is a draft for Alex):
# act1_arrival: a new game opens on the rain bus. She walks to the Welcome to Maple Grove sign, the
#   rain stops, the arrival music swells, the camera takes in the town (Hazel at her stall, Pip on
#   his round) and comes back to her face. Wren the mayor welcomes her ("we've been expecting you"),
#   walks her past the shops (Gus, Rosa, Theo, Hazel, Mabel) and up to Gran's house.
# act1_note (inside): Gran's note on the coffee table, kept in her bag; 100 coins; rent to Gran's tin.
# act1_yarn (her first yarn from Theo) → knit in the rocking chair → act1_knit (memory thread #1,
#   then bleating: two strays) → act1_strays (find them by the pond; meet Rowan; "you'll want a pen")
#   → act1_wood (her first wood from Gus: the pen builder, F, and gate crafting, G) → act1_pen (a
#   closed pen with a gate: "pen_built", the dog's cue) → herd them in → act1_flock ("sheep_penned")
#   → act1_market (Rosa buys the sweater) → act1_porch (the voicemail, Rowan's lantern) → end card.

== act1_arrival
@trigger start
@once
@weather rain
@home rowan 25.6 -5.5
@place nora 31.6 3.3 90
@prop bus bus 33.8 0.6 0
@prop suitcase case 32.2 3.6 20
@place hazel 58.5 -5.2 -45
@place pip 42.36 -7.6 180
@face pip 42.36 -9.0
@place wren 44.6 2.2 270
@fade out 0.01
@title Knitting Empire
@camera 32.6 2.2 10
@fade in 2.0
> Last stop. The rain has followed her all the way from the city.
@prop_move bus 72 0.6 6
> The bus pulls away and takes the last of the engine noise with it. One suitcase. A coat that was never meant for weather like this.
Nora (worried): Okay. Nobody followed. Nobody knows you're here.
@phone Unknown number
> Her phone buzzes. No name. It doesn't need one.
@camera nora 5
? The phone keeps ringing.
- Decline the call. -> declined | phone off; set declined_daniel
- Let it ring out. -> ringout | phone off; set ignored_daniel
@label declined
> She presses the red button, then holds the side button until the screen goes black. Her hand is shaking.
Nora (neutral): Not today. Not here.
@goto after
@label ringout
> She watches it ring until it stops. Then a little longer, in case.
Nora (sad): It'll stop. It has to stop eventually.
@label after
@prop_remove bus
> She hauls the suitcase up by its one good handle. Through the rain, up ahead, a painted sign.
@prop_remove case
@walk nora 36.2 2.4
@face nora 37.6 -1.2
@camera 37.6 -1.2 6
@wait 1.2
> WELCOME TO MAPLE GROVE. Someone keeps the paint fresh.
@weather clear
@music arrival
> And as she reads it, the rain stops. Just like that, like somebody turned off a tap.
@camera 50 -2 19
@wait 2.5
> Woodsmoke. Wet cobbles drying in the sun. Somewhere, bread.
@camera hazel 7 yaw -45
@wait 1.0
> Hazel the baker is selling the morning's loaves from her stall, still warm enough to steam.
@camera pip 7
@wait 1.0
> Pip the postman is on his round: a letter for every door, and a word for everyone who opens one.
@face nora 38.4 4.6
@camera nora 3 low yaw 45
@wait 1.0
Nora (warm): I think I'm going to like it here.
@walk wren 38.0 2.6
@face nora wren
@face wren nora
@camera between wren nora 7
Wren (happy): You must be Nora! Look at you, soaked through. Welcome to Maple Grove.
Nora (surprised): You know who I am?
Wren (warm): Wren. I'm the mayor, which mostly means I hold the spare keys and all the gossip. We've been expecting you, love.
Wren (warm): Your gran told the whole town you'd come home one day. Every Sunday, without fail.
Nora (sad): Did she.
Wren (happy): Come on. I'll show you round, and then I'll walk you up to the house. Leave the case, nobody here would dream of touching it.
@set act1_arrived
@home pip off
@walk gus 47.7 -9.1 nowait
@walk wren 45.8 -7.8 nowait
@walk nora 46.8 -7.6
@face nora gus
@face wren nora
@camera between gus nora 7.5
Wren (happy): Gus! Come and meet Ellie's granddaughter.
Gus (neutral): Builder's Delight. Timber, nails, rope, pots, anything that holds something else together. If I haven't got it, you don't need it.
Wren (wry): And if he has got it, it's under something else.
@face nora rosa
@camera between rosa nora 7.5
Rosa (happy): And I'm Rosa! The market's mine. If you make it, grow it or knit it, I'll sell it for you.
@walk theo 53.27 -9.2 nowait
@walk wren 52.2 -7.8 nowait
@walk nora 53.2 -7.6
@face nora theo
@face wren nora
@camera between theo nora 7.5
Theo (warm): Ellie's girl. You've got her chin. The Yarn Barn: yarn, needles, patterns, and the only decent kettle on the plaza.
Theo (wry): Your gran was my best customer for thirty years. And my worst payer.
@walk wren 56.0 -5.6 nowait
@walk nora 56.9 -5.2
@face nora hazel
@face hazel nora
@camera between hazel nora 7.5 yaw -45
Hazel (happy): New face! Here, this one's on the house. Don't argue, I've already buttered it.
Nora (warm): Thank you. It smells incredible.
@walk mabel 64.25 -7.4 nowait
@walk wren 63.0 -6.0 nowait
@walk nora 64.0 -5.8
@face nora mabel
@face wren nora
@camera between mabel nora 7.5
Mabel (warm): And that's Willow Homes, and I'm Mabel, and if you need papers signed or a piece of cake, I'm your woman.
Mabel (sad): I was sorry about Ellie, love. Half the town turned up for her. She'd knitted for most of us.
@fade out 0.8
@home hazel off
@home gus off
@home theo off
@home mabel off
@place nora 10.4 3.0 270
@place wren 11.2 2.0 270
@face wren nora
@face nora 8.0 3.0
@camera 9.6 2.8 8
@fade in 1.0
> Gran's house. Smaller than she remembers, and the roses have gone wild.
@face nora wren
Wren (warm): Here we are. Front door sticks: lift it and shove. She never fixed it, said it kept the salesmen out.
Wren (neutral): She left something for you, inside. I haven't looked. I'll leave you to it.
Nora (warm): Thank you, Wren. For all of it.
Wren (happy): Welcome home, Nora.
@walk wren 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 1.5
@home wren off
@set act1_toured
@goal Go inside Gran's house | 7.2 3.0
@camera player
@toast Click the ground to walk. Follow the gold marker.

== act1_note
@trigger area cottage_inside
@requires act1_toured
@once
@goal
@camera 3.6 2.6 9
> Dust on everything. The clock on the mantel stopped at twenty past four.
Nora (sad): Hi, Gran.
> It still smells like her. Lanolin and woodsmoke and the lemon drops she kept in her apron.
@walk nora 4.0 3.9
@face nora 4.0 3.0
@camera 4.0 3.0 4
> On the table, propped against an old biscuit tin, a folded note. Gran's handwriting, all loops and hurry.
Nora (surprised): "For my Nora."
@farm note
> "My darling Nora. I have missed you every single day since you moved away. The kettle still boils for two out of habit, and I let it."
> "The house is yours now, if you'll have it. Keep it warm for me. Put a little in the tin each week. Not because the house needs the money. Because a home you pay into is a home you stay in."
> "There's a hundred coins under the lid to start you off. Go and see Theo for some good yarn, and make something with your hands. It always helped me. It will help you."
> "Whatever happened out there, love, it stays out there. In here it's just you, and the kettle, and me in every cup. All my love, always. Gran."
Nora (sad): ...Okay. Okay, Gran.
> She folds the note into her pocket. Under the lid of the tin: a hundred coins, in neat little paper rolls.
@toast Gran's note is in your bag. Rent: 20c a week, into her tin on the table.
@set act1_note
@goal Buy yarn from Theo at the Yarn Barn | 53.27 -9.6
@camera player

== act1_yarn
@trigger event yarn_bought
@requires act1_note
@once
@goal
Nora (warm): Good yarn. Gran would approve. She'd also say I paid too much.
@set act1_yarn
@goal Knit your first sweater in Gran's rocking chair | 2.4 3.6
@toast Click the rocking chair and choose Knit.

== act1_knit
@trigger event knit_done
@requires act1_yarn
@once
@goal
# memory thread #1: the first thing she knits in years brings back the last thing she knit
@camera player 4
@memory on 1.6
> The last stitch closes. She holds the piece up to the window, and her hands remember another sweater.
> Navy, with a cream band across the chest. He'd said cream made him look soft, so she made the band thin.
Daniel: You made this? Babe. You know I don't really do wool.
> Four months of it. Evenings, mostly, after he'd gone to bed, so it would be a surprise.
Daniel: Don't make that face. It's sweet. It's just not... me.
> In the morning it was in the bin by the back door, under the coffee grounds. He said it must have fallen in.
> She didn't knit again for six years.
@memory off 1.6
@journal memory The navy sweater | Four months of evenings. A thin cream band, because cream made him look soft. It ended up in the bin under the coffee grounds and I didn't knit again for six years. Today I did.
Nora (sad): ...Okay. That one still stings.
@farm strays
> Somewhere outside, not far off, something says "baa". Then something else says it louder.
Nora (surprised): Sheep? Gran's flock went years ago.
@set act1_knit
@goal Find where that bleating is coming from | 13.5 -14
@camera player

== act1_strays
@trigger area strays
@requires act1_knit
@once
@goal
@home rowan 16.4 -12.2
@walk nora 12.2 -12.4
@face nora 13.5 -14
@camera 13.8 -13.4 8
> Two sheep, grazing past the pond like they own the place. No ear tags. Burrs in their wool.
@face rowan nora
@face nora rowan
@camera between rowan nora 6.5
Rowan (wry): Afternoon. Friends of yours?
Nora (surprised): I was about to ask you the same thing.
Rowan (neutral): Not mine. No marks on them. Strays off the ridge, I'd guess. They turn up every spring, looking for somebody soft.
Nora (wry): And they found me.
Rowan (neutral): Rowan. I keep the flock up on the hill. Ellie and I traded favours. Mostly she fed me and I fixed things.
Nora (neutral): Nora. The granddaughter. The one from the city.
Rowan (warm): I know. She talked about you. A lot, actually.
@walk rowan 14.8 -13.0
@anim rowan Work
@camera between rowan nora 7
@wait 0.6
@shake 0.5
> A dead branch gives under his boot with a crack like a gunshot.
Nora (surprised): Ah!
> Her whole body jerks. Her hands are up before she can stop them.
@anim rowan off
@face rowan nora
@face nora rowan
Rowan (worried): Hey. You alright?
? Rowan watches her, careful, the way you'd watch a skittish ewe.
- I'm fine. It just made me jump. -> fine | familiarity rowan +2; set nora_deflected
- Sorry. Loud noises. Long story. -> honest | trust rowan +3; familiarity rowan +2; set nora_opened
@label fine
Rowan (neutral): Right. Course.
> He doesn't push. He does kick the rest of the branch into the long grass, quietly.
@goto keep
@label honest
Rowan (warm): Nothing to be sorry for. I'll tread quieter.
Nora (warm): Thanks.
@label keep
Rowan (neutral): If you want them, they're yours. Finders keepers, out here. But you'll want a pen first, or they'll wander back the way they came.
Nora (worried): Gran's pen is long gone. I've never built anything in my life.
Rowan (wry): Panels, posts and a gate. Sheep lean on everything, so build it like you mean it. Gus at Builder's Delight sells timber.
? What do you say?
- I'll do it. Today. -> deal | familiarity rowan +3
- Could you help? -> nohelp | trust rowan +1; familiarity rowan +1
@label deal
Rowan (wry): Good. I'll come by and lean on it after. You bring tea.
@goto bye
@label nohelp
Rowan (warm): I'll talk you through it. It's your pen, though. That matters, with sheep.
@label bye
@set met_rowan
> He tips the crook at her like a hat and heads off up the hill, whistling at nothing.
@walk rowan 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 2.5
@home rowan off
@set act1_strays
@camera player
@goal Buy wood from Gus at Builder's Delight | 47.7 -9.4

== act1_wood
@trigger event wood_bought
@requires act1_strays
@once
@goal
Nora (neutral): Right. A pen. Panels, posts and a gate. How hard can it be.
@set act1_wood
@toast Press F (or Build pen) to lay fence panels: 1 wood each. Craft a gate (G) from 2 wood and set it in the fence.
@goal Build a pen with a gate, near the strays | 13.5 -14

== act1_pen
@trigger event pen_built
@requires act1_wood
@once
@goal
Nora (happy): A pen. An actual pen, with an actual gate. Gran, are you seeing this?
> Now the hard part. The strays are still out by the pond, and they don't look like they're in any hurry.
@toast Walk up behind the sheep and they'll move away from you. Steer them in through the gate.
@goal Herd the two strays into your pen

== act1_flock
@trigger event sheep_penned
@requires act1_wood
@once
@goal
@camera player 7
Nora (happy): Both of them. In!
> They're already eating the grass inside the pen as if they'd never been anywhere else.
Nora (warm): Welcome home, you two. That makes three of us.
@set act1_fence_done
@goal Take your sweater to Rosa at the Maple Grove market | 48.5 -5.6
@camera player

== act1_market
# scene 5: market day. Someone values her work, out loud, in public.
@trigger area market
@requires act1_fence_done
@once
@goal
@walk nora 48.5 -5.9
@face rosa nora
@face nora rosa
@camera between rosa nora 7
Rosa (surprised): Hold on. Hold ON. Is that hand-knit?
Nora (worried): It's nothing. It's a first try, the tension's all over the place—
Rosa (happy): Honey, I've sold factory jumpers for eleven years. I know nothing when I see it, and this isn't it.
> Rosa turns the sweater inside out, the way you'd check a melon.
Rosa (happy): Look at those floats. Look at them! Theo! THEO! Come and look at this!
@if has sweater -> sell
Rosa (warm): You've sold it already? Then bring me the next one, before anybody else sees it.
@goto theo
@label sell
@take sweater 1
@give coins 60
Rosa (warm): Sixty coins, and I want the next one before anybody else sees it.
@toast Sold your first sweater: +60 coins
@label theo
@walk theo 50.4 -6.0
@face theo nora
@face nora theo
@camera between theo nora 7
Theo (happy): Rosa doesn't shout for anybody. Last time she shouted it was a calf with two heads.
Theo (neutral): Told you. Ellie's granddaughter, through and through. She bought her wool off me for thirty years. Never once paid on time.
? Theo holds out a bundle of oatmeal yarn.
- I can't take that. Let me pay you. -> pay | familiarity theo +2
- Thank you. Really. -> thanks | trust theo +2; familiarity theo +2
@label pay
Theo (wry): You can. Later. That's what credit is. Ellie invented it, as far as I'm concerned.
@goto give
@label thanks
Theo (warm): Pay me when the sweaters sell. They will.
@label give
@give wool 5
@set theo_credit
> Five skeins. More than anyone's handed her in a long time, and it isn't even charity. It's a bet on her.
Nora (warm): Thank you. Both of you.
@journal note Market day | Rosa shouted across the whole plaza. Theo gave me wool on credit, like I'm someone worth betting on. Sixty coins for something I made with my own hands.
@time 18.5
@set act1_market
@camera player
@goal Head home. It's getting dark | 9.8 3.0

== act1_porch
# scene 6: the porch at night. She can open up a little or deflect; both are valid, and it sets
# the tone of her and Rowan's arc.
@trigger area porch
@requires act1_market
@once
@goal
@fade out 0.8
@time 21.5
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@camera 11.2 3.0 6
@fade in 1.2
> Night comes down fast out here. No streetlights. Just stars, and a porch light that hasn't worked since Gran.
@phone Voicemail: Claire Moss, family law
> One new voicemail. Her thumb hovers over it for a while. Then she plays it.
Voicemail: Hi Nora, it's Claire. Daniel's side has filed to contest the sale of the house.
Voicemail: It doesn't change much, honestly. But they want mediation. In person, in the city. Call me when you can. And take care of yourself, okay?
@phone off
Nora (sad): In person.
> She sits down by the bottom step. The wood is cold through her jeans.
@place rowan 15.0 4.8 270
@walk rowan 11.3 2.5
> A lantern bobs along the fence line, then stops.
@face rowan nora
@face nora rowan
@camera between rowan nora 6
Rowan (neutral): Checking your fence. It's holding. Mostly out of spite.
Rowan (worried): You okay?
? She could tell him. Some of it. Or none of it.
- Not really. My ex wants to drag this out. I thought I'd left it in the city. -> open | trust rowan +3; romance rowan +1; familiarity rowan +2; set nora_opened_porch
- I'm fine. Long day. -> deflect | familiarity rowan +1; set nora_deflected_porch
@label open
Rowan (neutral): Some things follow you. Took me two years to stop setting the table for two.
> He doesn't say anything else, and it's exactly the right amount.
Nora (warm): Thank you. For not saying something wise.
Rowan (wry): I don't know anything wise. Ask the sheep.
@goto lantern
@label deflect
Rowan (neutral): Right. Long days are the worst ones.
> He doesn't push. He never seems to.
@label lantern
> He sets the lantern down by the bottom step.
@prop lantern rowan_lantern 10.6 2.3 0
Rowan (warm): Ellie's porch light's been broken for years. Keep that. I know the way home in the dark.
@walk rowan 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 2.0
@journal note The porch | Claire called: Daniel wants mediation, in person. Rowan left his lantern by the step. I didn't ask him to.
@fade out 1.4
@home rowan off
@set act1_done
@title Act 1: Cast On
@sleep
@time 7.5
@weather clear
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@camera 12.4 3.0 9
@fade in 1.6
> Morning. In daylight the cottage looks smaller, and a little less sad. There's a lantern by the step.
@title to be continued
@camera player
@toast Act 1 complete. The farm is yours now.
